arm64: dts: h713: hy310 - crust as the ARISC firmware

The HY310 boots crust: TF-A starts it from the FIT, and the arisc driver
loads or keeps the same build from /lib/firmware. The DT named the vendor
image, so the driver held a running crust in reset and loaded the vendor
image over it (crust-20261007 review INT-02, K10, F13; W1 of the crust
release design). firmware-name index 0 becomes hy310-crust.bin - named
after the board, because the rootfs may be built without one and ships
the file only for a board whose FIT carries crust; index 1, the EDID,
stays.

The dtsi keeps the vendor name for the HY200 QZ713 V2, which includes it
directly. The HY300 Pro and the HY200 QZ713DF A1 include the HY310's file
and name the vendor image again: whether they get crust is the owner's
decision (question 7.2 g of the design), and nothing of theirs is
measured with it.

Not for the line before the rootfs ships /lib/firmware/hy310-crust.bin
from the same build as the FIT's scp (B2/B4) and the arisc driver keeps
a running crust: without the file, request_firmware fails, the arisc
probe with it, and hdmirx defers for good.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* The vendor ARISC image, as before: crust has run on the HY310 only. */
+&arisc {
+	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
+};
+
 &hdmirx {
 	allwinner,backlight-pwm-info = <5 1 40000 1 1 100>;
 };
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -35,6 +35,11 @@
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* The vendor ARISC image, as before: crust has run on the HY310 only. */
+&arisc {
+	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
+};
+
 /*
  * This board's display firmware keeps its event log 0xC00 below the HY310's:
  * the mode-1 ring at 0x4b27219c and the control block at 0x4b48b200, whose
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
@@ -54,3 +54,11 @@
 &motor_ctr { status = "okay"; };	/* range gate PH14 measured 12.09., see doku/94 */
 &adc_keys { status = "disabled"; };
 &board_mgr { status = "okay"; };	/* temperature + fan speed, see doku/60 */
+
+/*
+ * crust is this board's ARISC firmware: TF-A starts it from the FIT, and the
+ * driver finds the same build as hy310-crust.bin in /lib/firmware. The dtsi
+ * names the vendor image, and the two boards that include this file name it
+ * again.
+ */
+&arisc { firmware-name = "hy310-crust.bin", "hy310-edid.bin"; };
